    {
      "unitId": "unresolved-he-5ce0dcd4797cff6f67d7",
      "sourceRef": "Yevamot 62a",
      "beforeEnglishSHA256": "088ab22c04b3ea4254f890b5dd9f8ad18437e0133436dc8a4b4be61488e7f2b1",
      "proposedEnglish": "Rav Huna said: He has fulfilled the commandment, on account of Rav Asi’s teaching. For Rav Asi said: The son of David will not come until all the souls in the Guf [the treasury of souls] have been exhausted, as it is said: ‘For the spirit from before Me grows faint,’ and so forth. Rabbi Yochanan said: He has not fulfilled the commandment to be fruitful and multiply. We require ‘He formed it to be inhabited,’ and that is absent here.",
      "proposedEnglishSHA256": "ec393b370e844d3a0fcd11227498f38c434a4655c00440a6bab22a8385d36b09",
      "reason": "Preserve the source-origin min in מלפני. Grow faint itself is supported by saved primary Hebrew Rashi on Isaiah57:16.",
      "status": "accepted-and-verified-applied"
    },
    {
      "unitId": "unresolved-he-b2ee1b42ce31f56001fd",
      "sourceRef": "Berakhot 12b",
      "beforeEnglishSHA256": "94018de3c1db80a7b1fb068b35526172f7733d6d42647d50e670ff6297e2cf17",
      "proposedEnglish": "Rabbah bar Chinena the Elder said in the name of Rav: Anyone who commits a transgression and feels ashamed of it is forgiven for all his iniquities, as it is said: ‘So that you may remember and be ashamed, and no longer have an opening of the mouth because of your humiliation, when I atone for you for everything you have done, declares Hashem God.’",
      "proposedEnglishSHA256": "d5fe68a30a58235cc4a25bcf10af2942e97804943e4b620debc0e91894109dc0",
      "reason": "Follow the supplied ה׳ אֱלֹהִים and the established Hashem/God convention.",
      "status": "accepted-and-verified-applied"
    },
    {
      "unitId": "unresolved-he-173e654c31ec935c5b4c",
      "sourceRef": "Gittin 57a",
      "beforeEnglishSHA256": "59dd4c0f47e6d0cf7e2edb090e23a50818b0599da62e66609fb67e2b453226f5",
      "proposedEnglish": "Bar Daroma’s mouth caused him to stumble, and he said: ‘You, God, have surely abandoned us, and You, God, do not go out with our armies.’ But David said this too! David was speaking in astonishment.",
      "proposedEnglishSHA256": "17536832866fbd58ed5bdecdcaf701b2468179ccccbe3bde587864c8bdb667df",
      "reason": "Make Bar Daroma’s assertion distinct from David’s astonished question, as the source explicitly contrasts them.",
      "status": "accepted-and-verified-applied"
    }
  ],
